# the relocate phase: every relocation of a surviving section is applied to
# the bytes of the output section it landed in
#
# the bytes of every surviving input section are copied to where layout put
# them, the atoms collection dropped cut out. each relocation then finds its
# row in the set of the output format and architecture by its neutral kind,
# takes its addresses from the layout, the addresses of the GOT slot, PLT entry
# or copy its decision reaches, the thread-local anchors and the index of its
# target's output section from the records that publish them, and is applied
# through the relocation engine. a relocation the loader fills is recorded and
# left alone, one it moves is recorded and patched with its static value, and
# one whose target lies in dropped code is refused, unless it is in debug
# information, which only describes code and is left as it is. an undefined
# weak reference resolves by the format's rule. a relocatable output keeps its
# relocations, so its bytes are copied and not patched.

